dbooks\nGraduate School\nBiomedical Engineering\nCivil and Architectural Engineering\nChemical, Environmental, and Materials Engineering\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nCode of Conduct\nStudent Conduct\nStudent Rights and Responsibilities Handbook\nForms\nApproval of dissertation SACS B.S./M.S. Graduate Course Request\nAll other relevant forms for admission to candidacy, defense approval, and dissertation approval can be accessed via Dynamic Forms\nReady for your PhD Proposal?\nProcess for Proposal\nReady for your PhD Defense?\nProcess for Defense\nFunding for Conference Travel\nAll graduate students are eligible to apply for travel funding through the Graduate Activity Fee Allocation Committee (GAFAC) each year. See the GAFAC website to apply.\nThe Graduate School offers a one-time travel scholarship. See the Graduate School website for more information and eligibility.\nInternational Students\nFor more information for International Students, please visit the site for International Student and Scholar Services (ISSS)\nTax Filing Resources for International Students:\nEach year starting in February, International Student and Scholar Services (ISSS) provides guidance on IRS filing requirements and access to Glacier Tax Prep, a user-friendly online tax preparation program. This tool helps UM international students, scholars, and their dependents:\nDetermine their U.S. tax status\nComplete required IRS tax forms as non-residents for tax purposes\nStay tuned for ISSS communications in early spring for instructions and access details.\nIf you are an international student receiving a UM scholarship or award, please review the following tax-related information:\nScholarships or awards that exceed tuition and mandatory fees, or include student employment wages, may be subject to federal tax withholding.\nThe University of Miami Payroll and Accounting Department has prepared a detailed guide outlining your potential tax responsibilities.\nClick here to view the guide\nThis guide includes:\nScholarships and Awards exceeding tuition and fees\nRequirements for Student Employees\n1042\nFiling Your Income Tax Return\nHelpful Resources\nNew Student Information\nNew students looking for more information including FAQs and housing information should visit the links located below:\nNew Graduate Student Checklist\nHousing\nPhD Advisory Council (PAC)\nThe Ph.D. Advisory Council members serve as the official liaison between the PhD. Students in each department and the College of Engineering leadership. The role of the members is as follows:\nAdvocate for the academic, professional, and social interests of Ph.D. students.\nCommunicate student concerns, needs, and suggestions to the College leadership.\nProgram:\nRepresentative\nBiomedical Engineering\nJasmine Murray\nCivil and Architectural Engineering\nDanielle Bejar\nChemical, Environmental, and Materials Engineering\nBrittany Pellettiere\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nDefeng Zhou\nIndustrial and Systems Engineering\nAhmed Ali\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nRuben Escobar\nGraduate Student Association\nGraduate students looking for more information about the Graduate Student Association are encouraged to visit their site at the following location: https://um-gsa.org/\nFall 2026 Orientation Presentation\nView here\nQuestions? Concerns? Feedback?\nSubmit anonymous feedback here\nTop\nUniversity of Miami\nCoral Gables, FL 33124\n305-284-2211\nCollege of Engineering\n1251 Memorial Drive, McArthur Engineering Building\nCoral Gables,\nFL\n33146\n(305) 284-2404\n(305) 284-2404\nResources\nAbout UM\nmyUM\nCaneLink\nAcademic Calendar\nCanvas/Blackboard\nUM Network\nAlumni & Friends\nMedical Center\nHurricane Sports\nCareers\nSupport COE\nGive to COE\nWays to Give\nVisit\nCampus Map\nParking & Transportation\nConnect\nsocial-instagram\nsocial-linkedin\nsocial-twitter\nsocial-facebook\nCopyright: 2026 University of